   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project for Reintegration Assistance to Potential and Returned Migrants Youth Focused on Training and Entrepreneurship in Eastern El Salvador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To address the needs of the Government of El Salvador, and based on previous investments from the Government of Japan in the Eastern Region of the country, IOM proposes a project to enhance potential and returning migrant youth capabilities to improve their livelihood under a human security paradigm by providing market-driven vocational/entrepreneurship training, as well as upgrading education facilities to provide effective learning environments. The project is divided into three components: 1) Expand access to market-driven vocational/entrepreneurship trainings, and humanitarian assistance for potential and returning migrant youth; 2) Improve learning environments by enabling access for target population to safe, inclusive and eco-friendly facilities; 3) Support evidence-based decision making and collaboration among multiple stakeholders to advance comprehensive responses under a human security approach.</narrative>
  </description>
